* Test models of this project's own (no maker's text): parts that are neither an op-amp nor a lone
* transistor, written the ways makers write them: pins by number, by name, or told in a note.

* a 5 V series regulator, pins by number and no word about them
.SUBCKT TST7805 1 2 3
R1 1 4 1k
D1 2 4 DZ
Q1 1 4 3 QN
.MODEL DZ D(IS=1e-14 BV=5.6 IBV=1m RS=1)
.MODEL QN NPN(BF=200 IS=1e-14)
.ENDS

* the same regulator, its pins named
.SUBCKT TSTLDO OUT GND IN
R1 IN 4 1k
D1 GND 4 DZ
Q1 IN 4 OUT QN
.MODEL DZ D(IS=1e-14 BV=5.6 IBV=1m RS=1)
.MODEL QN NPN(BF=200 IS=1e-14)
.ENDS

* an adjustable regulator, 1.25 V from ADJ to OUT; its pins are told in the note above it
*                 ADJ OUT IN
.SUBCKT TST317    1   2   3
V1 5 1 1.25
R0 3 1 100k
E1 4 1 5 2 1000
Q1 3 4 2 QN
.MODEL QN NPN(BF=200 IS=1e-14)
.ENDS

* a 2.5 V shunt reference: reference, anode, cathode (by number)
.SUBCKT TST431 1 2 3
V1 4 2 2.5
G1 5 2 1 4 10
D1 3 5 DM
R1 1 2 10Meg
.MODEL DM D(IS=1e-12)
.ENDS

* an optocoupler: LED anode, LED cathode, emitter, collector (by number)
.SUBCKT OPTOTEST 1 2 3 4
R1 5 2 2
D1 1 5 LD
G1 4 6 5 2 1m
Q1 4 6 3 QN
.MODEL LD D(IS=1e-20)
.MODEL QN NPN(BF=500 IS=1e-14)
.ENDS

* a comparator with an open collector, in the usual order: + - V+ V- OUT
.SUBCKT TST393 1 2 3 4 5
R0 3 4 100k
G1 4 7 2 1 1m
R1 7 4 10k
D1 4 7 DM
Q1 5 7 4 QN
.MODEL DM D(IS=1e-12)
.MODEL QN NPN(BF=200 IS=1e-14)
.ENDS

* the same comparator, its maker's own order: OUT V- + - V+
.SUBCKT TST339 5 4 1 2 3
R0 3 4 100k
G1 4 7 2 1 1m
R1 7 4 10k
D1 4 7 DM
Q1 5 7 4 QN
.MODEL DM D(IS=1e-12)
.MODEL QN NPN(BF=200 IS=1e-14)
.ENDS

* a zener diode as a lone model
.MODEL BZXTEST D(IS=1e-14 BV=5.1 IBV=5m RS=2)

* three pins that are no regulator and no reference: two resistors
.SUBCKT TSTNET 1 2 3
R1 1 2 1k
R2 2 3 1k
.ENDS
